      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "It delivers a full record of requests and responses to Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) or Amazon CloudWatch .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/amazon-bedrock-tokenomics-data-lake/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:56:36.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T17:44:11.550Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "What is the Amazon Bedrock observability data lake?",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/amazon-bedrock-tokenomics-data-lake/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:56:36.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T17:44:11.550Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A centralized Amazon Bedrock invocation log data lake pulls raw model invocation logs from your linked accounts into Amazon CloudWatch .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/amazon-bedrock-tokenomics-data-lake/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:56:36.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T17:44:11.550Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The central account processes the data through Amazon Data Firehose , and exposes them through Amazon Athena as one clean table you can query across your organization.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/amazon-bedrock-tokenomics-data-lake/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:56:36.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T17:44:11.550Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 1: Amazon Bedrock invocation observability data lake architecture across a central account and linked accounts",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/amazon-bedrock-tokenomics-data-lake/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:56:36.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T17:44:11.550Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "How is the Amazon Bedrock data lake designed?",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/amazon-bedrock-tokenomics-data-lake/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:56:36.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T17:44:11.550Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The data lake moves each invocation through five stages, from the moment Amazon Bedrock writes a log to the point you can query it in Athena.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/amazon-bedrock-tokenomics-data-lake/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:56:36.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T17:44:11.550Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Amazon Data Firehose buffers the records and writes them to an Amazon S3 bucket, converting from JSON to Parquet on the way through.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/amazon-bedrock-tokenomics-data-lake/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-10T16:56:36.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T17:44:11.550Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Run a test invocation in a source account, wait for Amazon Data Firehose to flush its buffer ( roughly a minute, sometimes longer ), then confirm Parquet objects have appeared under the data lake’s data/ prefix.",
